    "labelChirho": "Naaman (personal name)",
    "descriptionChirho": "Proper masculine name referring primarily to Naaman the Syrian army commander healed of leprosy by Elisha (2 Kgs 5), as well as other biblical figures bearing this name (Gen 46:21, Num 26:40, 1 Chr 8:4). Transliterated consistently: eng 'Naaman', spa 'Naamán', arb 'نعمان', kor '나아만', swa 'Naamani', hin 'नामान'. The two clusters differ only by the presence of the conjunction waw prefix, not by referent or meaning.",
